      "problem": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to \\infty}\\dfrac{x}{\\ln{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty.$ However, since $x \\gg \\ln{x}$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}\\dfrac{x}{\\ln{x}} = \\infty.\n$$",
